DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     hhttppaasssswwdd is used to create and update user authentication files for HTTP
     daemons.

     The options are as follows:

     --II      Switch to batch mode.  hhttppaasssswwdd reads exactly one line from stan‐
             dard input and splits it at the first ":".  The first part is the
             login, the second part is the password which hhttppaasssswwdd then hashes
             using bcrypt(3).

     hhttppaasssswwdd prompts for a password and generates a hash using bcrypt(3).  A
     line suitable for a password file is written to the standard output.  If
     invoked with two arguments (or one argument if the --II flag is used), user
     authentication _f_i_l_e is updated.

